./research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md:118:- **Why the inequality is strict here.** Equality in [[thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral]] would require the integrand to point in a fixed direction, and $f(t) = (1,t,t^{2})$ changes direction as $t$ runs over $[0,1]$. That heuristic is not what is proved above: the proof separates the two sides by an explicit numerical bound, which is the only argument available at this point in the reading order.
