./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14691:def-oriented-integral
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14842:[L2] If $h$ is integrable then $\int_a^b h$ is the common value of the lower and upper integrals ([[def-darboux-integral]], [[def-infimum]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14848:[L5] With oriented limits, $\int_v^u h = -\int_u^v h$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14873:[L3] For a partition $R = (n,t)$ and bounded $h$: $L(h,R) = \sum_{i<n}m_i\Delta_i$, $U(h,R) = \sum_{i<n}M_i\Delta_i$, and $L(h,R) \le \underline{\int} h \le \overline{\int} h \le U(h,R)$, the integral being the common value of the two when they agree ([[def-darboux-sums]], [[def-darboux-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14881:[L7] With oriented limits, $\int_v^u h = -\int_u^v h$ and $\int_u^u h = 0$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14928:[L8] Oriented limits are not needed here, $a < b$ throughout; $\int_a^a u = 0$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14963:[L3] $\underline{\int_a^b} f = \sup_P L(f,P)$ and $\overline{\int_a^b} f = \inf_P U(f,P)$, and $f$ integrable means the two agree, their common value being $\int_a^b f$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:14973:[L8] Oriented limits are not needed here, $a<b$ throughout ([[def-oriented-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:15008:[L7] Oriented limits are not needed here, $a<b$ throughout ([[def-oriented-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:15039:[L5] $\underline{\int_0^1} u = \sup_P L(u,P)$ and $\overline{\int_0^1} u = \inf_P U(u,P)$; $u$ is integrable exactly when the two agree ([[def-darboux-integral]], [[def-bounded-set]]).
