./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:19995:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:20065:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $f + g$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b (f+g) = \\int_a^b f + \\int_a^b g$;\n2. for every real $\\lambda$, $\\lambda f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b \\lambda f = \\lambda \\int_a^b f$;\n3. consequently, for all reals $\\lambda, \\mu$ the function $\\lambda f + \\mu g$ is\n   integrable and\n   $$\\int_a^b(\\lambda f + \\mu g) \\;=\\; \\lambda\\int_a^b f \\;+\\; \\mu\\int_a^b g ;$$\n4. the same identity holds with oriented limits: if $u, v \\in [a,b]$ and $f, g$\n   are integrable between $u$ and $v$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]), then\n   $\\int_u^v(\\lambda f + \\mu g) = \\lambda\\int_u^v f + \\mu\\int_u^v g$.",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:20373:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then $f$ is Darboux integrable on $[a,b]$\n([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if**",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:20381:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:20822:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $f + g$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b (f+g) = \\int_a^b f + \\int_a^b g$;\n2. for every real $\\lambda$, $\\lambda f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b \\lambda f = \\lambda \\int_a^b f$;\n3. consequently, for all reals $\\lambda, \\mu$ the function $\\lambda f + \\mu g$ is\n   integrable and\n   $$\\int_a^b(\\lambda f + \\mu g) \\;=\\; \\lambda\\int_a^b f \\;+\\; \\mu\\int_a^b g ;$$\n4. the same identity holds with oriented limits: if $u, v \\in [a,b]$ and $f, g$\n   are integrable between $u$ and $v$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]), then\n   $\\int_u^v(\\lambda f + \\mu g) = \\lambda\\int_u^v f + \\mu\\int_u^v g$.",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:20835:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:20920:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21157:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21166:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $|f|$, $f^{2}$ and $fg$ are integrable on $[a,b]$\n   ([[def-abs-value]], [[def-integer-power]]);\n2. $\\max(f,g)$ and $\\min(f,g)$, defined pointwise\n   ([[def-max-min]]), are integrable on $[a,b]$;\n3. the **triangle inequality for the integral**:\n   $$\\Bigl|\\int_a^b f\\Bigr| \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b |f| .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21175:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21185:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $f + g$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b (f+g) = \\int_a^b f + \\int_a^b g$;\n2. for every real $\\lambda$, $\\lambda f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b \\lambda f = \\lambda \\int_a^b f$;\n3. consequently, for all reals $\\lambda, \\mu$ the function $\\lambda f + \\mu g$ is\n   integrable and\n   $$\\int_a^b(\\lambda f + \\mu g) \\;=\\; \\lambda\\int_a^b f \\;+\\; \\mu\\int_a^b g ;$$\n4. the same identity holds with oriented limits: if $u, v \\in [a,b]$ and $f, g$\n   are integrable between $u$ and $v$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]), then\n   $\\int_u^v(\\lambda f + \\mu g) = \\lambda\\int_u^v f + \\mu\\int_u^v g$.",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21231:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21409:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $|f|$, $f^{2}$ and $fg$ are integrable on $[a,b]$\n   ([[def-abs-value]], [[def-integer-power]]);\n2. $\\max(f,g)$ and $\\min(f,g)$, defined pointwise\n   ([[def-max-min]]), are integrable on $[a,b]$;\n3. the **triangle inequality for the integral**:\n   $$\\Bigl|\\int_a^b f\\Bigr| \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b |f| .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21418:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21434:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21654:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21702:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]), and let $c, d$ satisfy",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21724:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $f + g$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b (f+g) = \\int_a^b f + \\int_a^b g$;\n2. for every real $\\lambda$, $\\lambda f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b \\lambda f = \\lambda \\int_a^b f$;\n3. consequently, for all reals $\\lambda, \\mu$ the function $\\lambda f + \\mu g$ is\n   integrable and\n   $$\\int_a^b(\\lambda f + \\mu g) \\;=\\; \\lambda\\int_a^b f \\;+\\; \\mu\\int_a^b g ;$$\n4. the same identity holds with oriented limits: if $u, v \\in [a,b]$ and $f, g$\n   are integrable between $u$ and $v$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]), then\n   $\\int_u^v(\\lambda f + \\mu g) = \\lambda\\int_u^v f + \\mu\\int_u^v g$.",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21735:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $|f|$, $f^{2}$ and $fg$ are integrable on $[a,b]$\n   ([[def-abs-value]], [[def-integer-power]]);\n2. $\\max(f,g)$ and $\\min(f,g)$, defined pointwise\n   ([[def-max-min]]), are integrable on $[a,b]$;\n3. the **triangle inequality for the integral**:\n   $$\\Bigl|\\int_a^b f\\Bigr| \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b |f| .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21746:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:21754:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22004:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22090:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22215:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22237:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22261:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22273:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22283:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]), let $F$ be its integral function\n([[def-the-integral-function]]), and let $c \\in [a,b]$ be a point at which $f$ is\ncontinuous ([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $F$ is differentiable at $c$ as a\nfunction on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]) and",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22310:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22618:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22627:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $|f|$, $f^{2}$ and $fg$ are integrable on $[a,b]$\n   ([[def-abs-value]], [[def-integer-power]]);\n2. $\\max(f,g)$ and $\\min(f,g)$, defined pointwise\n   ([[def-max-min]]), are integrable on $[a,b]$;\n3. the **triangle inequality for the integral**:\n   $$\\Bigl|\\int_a^b f\\Bigr| \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b |f| .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22636:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $f + g$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b (f+g) = \\int_a^b f + \\int_a^b g$;\n2. for every real $\\lambda$, $\\lambda f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b \\lambda f = \\lambda \\int_a^b f$;\n3. consequently, for all reals $\\lambda, \\mu$ the function $\\lambda f + \\mu g$ is\n   integrable and\n   $$\\int_a^b(\\lambda f + \\mu g) \\;=\\; \\lambda\\int_a^b f \\;+\\; \\mu\\int_a^b g ;$$\n4. the same identity holds with oriented limits: if $u, v \\in [a,b]$ and $f, g$\n   are integrable between $u$ and $v$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]), then\n   $\\int_u^v(\\lambda f + \\mu g) = \\lambda\\int_u^v f + \\mu\\int_u^v g$.",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22645:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22652:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22784:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22820:     "quote": "Let $I \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ be order-convex with at least two elements\n([[def-interval]]) and let $f : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $I$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Call $G : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ a **primitive of $f$ on\n$I$** when $G$ is differentiable at every point of $I$ as a function on $I$ with\n$G' = f$ there ([[def-derivative]]). Then:\n\n1. **Existence.** Fix $c_0 \\in I$. The function\n   $$F : I \\to \\mathbb{R}, \\qquad F(x) \\;:=\\; \\int_{c_0}^x f$$\n   is defined at every $x \\in I$ ([[def-oriented-integral]],\n   [[def-the-integral-function]]) and is a primitive of $f$ on $I$.\n2. **Uniqueness up to a constant.** If $G_1$ and $G_2$ are primitives of $f$ on\n   $I$ then there is a real $k$ with $G_1(x) = G_2(x) + k$ for every $x \\in I$.\n3. **Evaluation.** If $a, b \\in I$ with $a < b$ and $G$ is any primitive of $f$\n   on $I$, then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; G(b) - G(a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22884:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $|f|$, $f^{2}$ and $fg$ are integrable on $[a,b]$\n   ([[def-abs-value]], [[def-integer-power]]);\n2. $\\max(f,g)$ and $\\min(f,g)$, defined pointwise\n   ([[def-max-min]]), are integrable on $[a,b]$;\n3. the **triangle inequality for the integral**:\n   $$\\Bigl|\\int_a^b f\\Bigr| \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b |f| .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22893:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:22900:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23056:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be monotone, that is\nnondecreasing or nonincreasing on $[a,b]$ ([[def-monotone-function]]). Then $f$\nis bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann integrable on $[a,b]$\n([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23092:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $|f|$, $f^{2}$ and $fg$ are integrable on $[a,b]$\n   ([[def-abs-value]], [[def-integer-power]]);\n2. $\\max(f,g)$ and $\\min(f,g)$, defined pointwise\n   ([[def-max-min]]), are integrable on $[a,b]$;\n3. the **triangle inequality for the integral**:\n   $$\\Bigl|\\int_a^b f\\Bigr| \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b |f| .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23132:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23145:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23329:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23662:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23672:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]), and let $c, d$ satisfy",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23680:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23701:     "quote": "Claim 3 is where [[def-oriented-integral]] earns its place: it holds for every\narrangement of the three points, including the degenerate ones, and it is the\nform used everywhere below.",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23708:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23719:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23935:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be monotone, that is\nnondecreasing or nonincreasing on $[a,b]$ ([[def-monotone-function]]). Then $f$\nis bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann integrable on $[a,b]$\n([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23963:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23975:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:23995:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24002:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24320:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24327:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24338:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24347:     "quote": "Let $I \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ be order-convex with at least two elements\n([[def-interval]]) and let $f : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $I$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Call $G : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ a **primitive of $f$ on\n$I$** when $G$ is differentiable at every point of $I$ as a function on $I$ with\n$G' = f$ there ([[def-derivative]]). Then:\n\n1. **Existence.** Fix $c_0 \\in I$. The function\n   $$F : I \\to \\mathbb{R}, \\qquad F(x) \\;:=\\; \\int_{c_0}^x f$$\n   is defined at every $x \\in I$ ([[def-oriented-integral]],\n   [[def-the-integral-function]]) and is a primitive of $f$ on $I$.\n2. **Uniqueness up to a constant.** If $G_1$ and $G_2$ are primitives of $f$ on\n   $I$ then there is a real $k$ with $G_1(x) = G_2(x) + k$ for every $x \\in I$.\n3. **Evaluation.** If $a, b \\in I$ with $a < b$ and $G$ is any primitive of $f$\n   on $I$, then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; G(b) - G(a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24414:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24452:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24454:     "quote": "([[def-interval]]). Let $f$ be a real-valued function whose domain contains that\ninterval. Say that **$f$ is integrable between $u$ and $v$** when either $u = v$,\nor $u \\ne v$ and the restriction of $f$ to $[u \\wedge v,\\ u \\vee v]$ is bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]) and Darboux integrable there ([[def-darboux-integral]],\n[[def-darboux-sums]]). For such $f$ define",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24602:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be monotone, that is\nnondecreasing or nonincreasing on $[a,b]$ ([[def-monotone-function]]). Then $f$\nis bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann integrable on $[a,b]$\n([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24618:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24629:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24636:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24665:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:24959:     "quote": "which is defined for every $N$: for $N \\ge 1$ the restriction of $f$ to $[0,N]$\nis monotone, hence bounded and integrable ([[thm-monotone-implies-integrable]]),\nand $J_0 = \\int_0^0 f = 0$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]). Here $N$ inside the\nintegral means the canonical natural $\\iota(N) \\in \\mathbb{R}$\n([[def-canonical-natural]]), as everywhere in this library. Let\n$s_N := \\sum_{k<N} f(k)$ be the partial sums of $\\sum_k f(k)$\n([[def-series]], [[def-finite-sum]]), the index $k$ ranging over $\\mathbb{N}$,\nwhich **contains $0$**. Then:\n\n1. **The bracket.** For every $N \\in \\mathbb{N}$,\n   $$J_N \\;\\le\\; s_N \\;\\le\\; f(0) + J_N .$$\n2. **The test.** $(J_N)_{N\\in\\mathbb{N}}$ is nondecreasing, and $\\sum_k f(k)$\n   converges **if and only if** the set $\\{\\,J_N : N \\in \\mathbb{N}\\,\\}$ is\n   bounded above ([[def-bounded-set]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25071:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25080:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25089:     "quote": "Let $I \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ be order-convex with at least two elements\n([[def-interval]]) and let $f : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $I$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Call $G : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ a **primitive of $f$ on\n$I$** when $G$ is differentiable at every point of $I$ as a function on $I$ with\n$G' = f$ there ([[def-derivative]]). Then:\n\n1. **Existence.** Fix $c_0 \\in I$. The function\n   $$F : I \\to \\mathbb{R}, \\qquad F(x) \\;:=\\; \\int_{c_0}^x f$$\n   is defined at every $x \\in I$ ([[def-oriented-integral]],\n   [[def-the-integral-function]]) and is a primitive of $f$ on $I$.\n2. **Uniqueness up to a constant.** If $G_1$ and $G_2$ are primitives of $f$ on\n   $I$ then there is a real $k$ with $G_1(x) = G_2(x) + k$ for every $x \\in I$.\n3. **Evaluation.** If $a, b \\in I$ with $a < b$ and $G$ is any primitive of $f$\n   on $I$, then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; G(b) - G(a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25105:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25464:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25480:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25491:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25499:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25529:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25776:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Suppose there are $r \\in \\mathbb{N}$ and points\n$d_0, \\dots, d_{r-1} \\in [a,b]$ such that $f$ is continuous\n([[def-continuity-real]]) at every point of $[a,b]$ other than\n$d_0, \\dots, d_{r-1}$; that is, every discontinuity of $f$\n([[def-classification-of-discontinuities]]) occurs among those $r$ listed\npoints. Then $f$ is Riemann integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25792:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25832:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:25840:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:26416:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:26504:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:26869:     "quote": "([[def-continuity-real]], [[def-classification-of-discontinuities]]) is at most\ncountable ([[def-countable]]), then $f$ is Riemann integrable on $[a,b]$\n([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:26885:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:26896:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be monotone, that is\nnondecreasing or nonincreasing on $[a,b]$ ([[def-monotone-function]]). Then $f$\nis bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann integrable on $[a,b]$\n([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27193:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27488:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27495:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27506:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27514:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27526:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27536:     "quote": "Let $I \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ be order-convex with at least two elements\n([[def-interval]]) and let $f : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $I$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Call $G : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ a **primitive of $f$ on\n$I$** when $G$ is differentiable at every point of $I$ as a function on $I$ with\n$G' = f$ there ([[def-derivative]]). Then:\n\n1. **Existence.** Fix $c_0 \\in I$. The function\n   $$F : I \\to \\mathbb{R}, \\qquad F(x) \\;:=\\; \\int_{c_0}^x f$$\n   is defined at every $x \\in I$ ([[def-oriented-integral]],\n   [[def-the-integral-function]]) and is a primitive of $f$ on $I$.\n2. **Uniqueness up to a constant.** If $G_1$ and $G_2$ are primitives of $f$ on\n   $I$ then there is a real $k$ with $G_1(x) = G_2(x) + k$ for every $x \\in I$.\n3. **Evaluation.** If $a, b \\in I$ with $a < b$ and $G$ is any primitive of $f$\n   on $I$, then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; G(b) - G(a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27644:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $f + g$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b (f+g) = \\int_a^b f + \\int_a^b g$;\n2. for every real $\\lambda$, $\\lambda f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ and\n   $\\int_a^b \\lambda f = \\lambda \\int_a^b f$;\n3. consequently, for all reals $\\lambda, \\mu$ the function $\\lambda f + \\mu g$ is\n   integrable and\n   $$\\int_a^b(\\lambda f + \\mu g) \\;=\\; \\lambda\\int_a^b f \\;+\\; \\mu\\int_a^b g ;$$\n4. the same identity holds with oriented limits: if $u, v \\in [a,b]$ and $f, g$\n   are integrable between $u$ and $v$ ([[def-oriented-integral]]), then\n   $\\int_u^v(\\lambda f + \\mu g) = \\lambda\\int_u^v f + \\mu\\int_u^v g$.",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27826:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27833:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27844:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. $|f|$, $f^{2}$ and $fg$ are integrable on $[a,b]$\n   ([[def-abs-value]], [[def-integer-power]]);\n2. $\\max(f,g)$ and $\\min(f,g)$, defined pointwise\n   ([[def-max-min]]), are integrable on $[a,b]$;\n3. the **triangle inequality for the integral**:\n   $$\\Bigl|\\int_a^b f\\Bigr| \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b |f| .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27883:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $G : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be differentiable at every\npoint of $[a,b]$ as a function on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]; at $a$ and $b$\nthis is the one-sided derivative), let $f := G'$, and suppose $f$ is integrable\non $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27893:     "quote": "Let $I \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$ be order-convex with at least two elements\n([[def-interval]]) and let $f : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $I$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Call $G : I \\to \\mathbb{R}$ a **primitive of $f$ on\n$I$** when $G$ is differentiable at every point of $I$ as a function on $I$ with\n$G' = f$ there ([[def-derivative]]). Then:\n\n1. **Existence.** Fix $c_0 \\in I$. The function\n   $$F : I \\to \\mathbb{R}, \\qquad F(x) \\;:=\\; \\int_{c_0}^x f$$\n   is defined at every $x \\in I$ ([[def-oriented-integral]],\n   [[def-the-integral-function]]) and is a primitive of $f$ on $I$.\n2. **Uniqueness up to a constant.** If $G_1$ and $G_2$ are primitives of $f$ on\n   $I$ then there is a real $k$ with $G_1(x) = G_2(x) + k$ for every $x \\in I$.\n3. **Evaluation.** If $a, b \\in I$ with $a < b$ and $G$ is any primitive of $f$\n   on $I$, then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; G(b) - G(a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27959:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27993:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:27995:     "quote": "([[def-interval]]). Let $f$ be a real-valued function whose domain contains that\ninterval. Say that **$f$ is integrable between $u$ and $v$** when either $u = v$,\nor $u \\ne v$ and the restriction of $f$ to $[u \\wedge v,\\ u \\vee v]$ is bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]) and Darboux integrable there ([[def-darboux-integral]],\n[[def-darboux-sums]]). For such $f$ define",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28190:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28206:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28233:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28590:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be continuous on $[a,b]$\n([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $f$ is bounded ([[def-bounded-set]]) and Riemann\nintegrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]).",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28597:     "source": "def-darboux-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28608:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals, let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]), let $F$ be its integral function\n([[def-the-integral-function]]), and let $c \\in [a,b]$ be a point at which $f$ is\ncontinuous ([[def-continuity-real]]). Then $F$ is differentiable at $c$ as a\nfunction on $[a,b]$ ([[def-derivative]]) and",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28620:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). The **integral function of $f$ with base point $a$**\nis",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28632:     "quote": "Let $a < c < b$ be reals and let $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be bounded\n([[def-bounded-set]]). Then:\n\n1. $f$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ ([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if** its\n   restrictions to $[a,c]$ and to $[c,b]$ are integrable;\n2. and in that case\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;=\\; \\int_a^c f \\;+\\; \\int_c^b f .$$\n3. **Oriented form.** Let $\\alpha < \\beta$ be reals, let $f : [\\alpha,\\beta] \\to\n   \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable, and let $u, v, w \\in [\\alpha,\\beta]$ be arbitrary.\n   Then, with the convention of [[def-oriented-integral]],\n   $$\\int_u^v f \\;+\\; \\int_v^w f \\;=\\; \\int_u^w f .$$",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28642:     "source": "def-oriented-integral",
./research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:28665:     "quote": "Let $a < b$ be reals and let $f, g : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be integrable\n([[def-darboux-integral]]). Then:\n\n1. **Nonnegativity.** If $f(x) \\ge 0$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $\\int_a^b f \\ge 0$.\n2. **Monotonicity.** If $f(x) \\le g(x)$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$ then\n   $$\\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b g .$$\n3. **Two-sided bound.** If $m \\le f(x) \\le M$ for every $x \\in [a,b]$, with\n   $m, M$ real, then\n   $$m\\,(b-a) \\;\\le\\; \\int_a^b f \\;\\le\\; M\\,(b-a) .$$",
