./research/audit/wave10-refuter-tasks/lem-integral-elementary-bounds.md:1796:([[def-darboux-integral]]) with $f(x) \ge 0$ for every $x \in [a,b]$ and
./research/audit/wave10-refuter-tasks/lem-integral-elementary-bounds.md:1824:[L7] $L(t,P) = \sum_{i<n}m_i\Delta_i$ with $m_i = \inf t[I_i]$; $\underline{\int_0^1} t$ is the supremum of the lower sums, $\overline{\int_0^1} t$ the infimum of the upper sums, and the integral is their common value when they agree ([[def-darboux-sums]], [[def-darboux-integral]]).
./research/audit/wave10-refuter-tasks/lem-integral-elementary-bounds.md:2205:deps: [def-darboux-sums, def-darboux-integral, lem-refinement-inequalities, lem-sup-epsilon, lem-inf-epsilon, def-partition-and-refinement, def-bounded-set, def-infimum, def-complete-ordered-field, def-ordered-field, lem-of-add-order, lem-of-sign-rules]
./research/audit/wave10-refuter-tasks/lem-integral-elementary-bounds.md:2238:([[def-darboux-integral]]) **if and only if**
./research/audit/wave10-refuter-tasks/lem-integral-elementary-bounds.md:2257:[L1] $L(f,P) \le \underline{\int_a^b} f \le \overline{\int_a^b} f \le U(f,P)$ for every partition $P$; $\underline{\int_a^b} f = \sup \mathcal{L}$ and $\overline{\int_a^b} f = \inf \mathcal{U}$ over the nonempty sets $\mathcal{L}$ of lower sums and $\mathcal{U}$ of upper sums; $f$ is integrable exactly when the two are equal ([[def-darboux-integral]], [[def-darboux-sums]]).
