items/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md:76:[L6] $\lVert f(t)\rVert_2$ is integrable on $[0,1]$ and $\bigl\lVert\int_0^1 f\bigr\rVert_2 \le \int_0^1\lVert f\rVert_2$ ([[thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral]], [[def-norm-and-normed-space]]).
items/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-77-
items/ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.md-78-[L7] Square roots and squaring: $\sqrt{c}$ is the unique nonnegative $s$ with $s^{2} = c$, and for $a,b \ge 0$, $a \le b$ exactly when $a^{2} \le b^{2}$ ([[thm-of-square-roots]], [[lem-of-square-monotone]]).
